  "How_to_play": "How to play?",
  "How_to_play_explain": "In the game, any disks of the opponent's color that are in a straight line and bounded by the disk just placed and another disk of the current player's color are turned over to the current player's color. The objective of the game is to have the majority of disks turned to display one's color when the last playable empty square is filled.",
  "HowToMoveTitle": "Make a move",
  "HowToMoveBody": "Place a disk on an empty square so that one or more opposing disks are trapped in a straight horizontal, vertical, or diagonal line between your new disk and another one of your disks. All trapped disks flip to your color.",
  "HowToTurnsTitle": "Take turns",
  "HowToTurnsBody": "Black moves first. If a player has no legal move, their turn is passed automatically. The game continues until neither player can move.",
  "HowToWinTitle": "Finish with the most disks",
  "HowToWinBody": "The game ends when the board is full or neither side has a legal move. The player with more disks on the board wins.",
  "HowToTipsTitle": "Strategy tips",
  "HowToTipsBody": "Corners can never be flipped, so work toward them carefully. Avoid giving away squares beside an open corner. Mobility matters: try to keep several legal moves available while limiting your opponent's choices.",
  "HowToControlsTitle": "Game controls",
  "HowToControlsBody": "Undo returns to the position before your last move. Hint highlights legal squares. Restart begins the same game setup again. Settings changes sound, haptics, and theme. Home returns to the beginning screen.",
